Table~\ref{tab:oracle} reports the results. All three oracle variants achieve \emph{lower} CAR than both unrefined baselines. The best oracle (Oracle-feature, 76.9\%) falls 5.1 points below LoRA (82.0\%) and 6.1 points below Full-FT (83.0\%). Oracle-adaptive and Oracle-fixed perform worse still at 75.0\% and 73.1\%. Refinement with perfect distance information produces more collisions than doing nothing. Fake safe rates confirm that oracle refinement does not reduce action collapse: Oracle-adaptive and Oracle-fixed both register 98.3\% (118/120 and 115/117 safe episodes), Oracle-feature registers 96.7\% (119/123). Ground-truth gradients redirect near-zero motion into near-zero motion in a different direction; they cannot generate viable trajectories from a collapsed policy.

